  <items>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp115438432">mearal</headword>
      <description>Notes: “sàl is uisge ’n ceann a chéile”. Applecross: “Cho saillt ris a’ mheireal”.</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp115464352">stragaidh (n.)</headword>
      <description>Notes: used of the catch of fish in a net.</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp115475368">sùireadh</headword>
      <description>Notes: favourable current in towards shore, against main current. (&lt; sùgh + ruith?)</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp115479760">abartach</headword>
      <description>Quotation: duine abartach. Notes: Duine nach b’urrainn rud a chumail aige fhéin.</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp115478896">cuaireadh</headword>
      <description>Quotation: Cuaireadh ort! Notes: mild malediction.</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp161846912">diridh-oichinn</headword>
      <description>Quotation: Dé ’n diridh-oichinn a th’ort? Notes: used of person running about from one thing to another.</description>
    </item>
	<item><headword id="idola1000" type="heading" level="h1">Rev. Norman MacSween, Kinloch, Lewis (Scalpay), 1979</headword></item>
	<item>
      <headword id="idp161843672">cnothag</headword>
      <description>Quotation: An ròs a’ tighinn ás a’ chnothaig. Notes: a bud.</description>
    </item>
